  "hint": "Strips going up end with right turns, and strips going down end with left turns. A bool like up can remember which way you're going, and up = !up flips it. Also, three turnRight()s face the same way as one turnLeft().",
  "solution": "#include \"Rover.h\"\n\nbool goingUp = true;\n\nvoid turn() {\n  if (goingUp) {\n    turnRight();\n  } else {\n    turnLeft();\n  }\n}\n\nvoid setup() {\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  while (distanceAhead() > 0) {\n    forward(1);\n  }\n  turn();\n  forward(1);\n  turn();\n  goingUp = !goingUp;\n}\n"
